  "text": "proprium.sanctorum-innocentium-martyrum-collecta",
  "about": "The collecta of the formulary “The Holy Innocents, Martyrs” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "O God, Whose praise the Innocents, Your martyrs, this day proclaimed, not by speaking, but by dying, put to death in us all the wickedness of sin, so that Your faith which our tongue professes may be proclaimed also by our life. Through our Lord Jesus Christ, Thy Son, who liveth and reigneth with Thee in the unity of the Holy Ghost, God, world without end. Amen." }
